  "note": "First election after the council was restored: it had been dissolved by an order of 13 April 1922 and run by a commissioner, Colonel Henry Waring (Belfast Gazette, 12 January 1923). The Unionists put forward no candidate; a meeting of Keady Nationalists and Sinn Féiners decided to nominate nine candidates willing to sign the declaration of loyalty, and they were nominated and declared elected. Thomas Mallon had been chairman in 1920 and Bernard Woods chairman when the council was dissolved."
